  "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
  "extraction_notes": "Table 4 of 4. Marks were derived twice and cross-checked: (a) pdftotext -bbox token centres binned to the six raster-derived column bands, and (b) a near-black pixel count (<90 intensity) inside every row-band x column-band rectangle. The two matrices agree on all 4 columns x 39 body rows with no disagreements; marked cells return 76-89 dark pixels and empty cells return 0. All four declared pages (43, 44, 45, 46) contribute activity rows: 15, 12, 10 and 2 respectively."
 },
 "table_metadata": {
  "table_number": 4,
  "table_type": "track",
  "table_title": "Table 4. Schedule of Activities for Early Termination, Unscheduled Visits, and Post-Treatment Follow-Up Period",
  "table_purpose": "Procedures at an early termination visit (ETV) and at unscheduled visits (V997), plus the post-treatment follow-up visits V801 and V802, for participants leaving any of the study's three main timelines.",
  "page_start": 43,
  "page_end": 46,
  "track_label": "Early Termination / Unscheduled / Post-Treatment",
  "notes": "Single leading label column (L=1); the first data column is position 2 (ETV=2, V997=3, V801=4, V802=5). The right-hand Comment column is position 6 and is treated as a notes column per prompt section 6: it is neither a schedule column nor an activity, so no schedule_grid or activity_schedule entries are emitted for position 6 and each non-empty Comment cell becomes a footnote annotation. table_type=track and track_label are taken as given from the boundary agent's structure and agree with my own reading: the four encounter columns (ETV, V997, V801, V802) exist in no other table, the table is the shared destination for participants leaving Tables 1-3, and it is not finer-grained timing for a single existing activity, so it is neither domain nor subsidiary. Column boundaries and row bands were recovered from the 200 dpi raster (vertical rules at 71.8 / 292.3 / 330.7 / 365.8 / 413.6 / 466.6 / 737.8 pt); row bands were read from the Comment column, never from the redacted label cells. The text layer of document pages 43-45 is glyph-spread (one glyph per token), so every activity name and annotation text on those pages was rebuilt by word re-segmentation and then checked character-for-character (whitespace removed) against the raw glyph stream; document page 46 has a clean text layer and supplied the verbatim wording of the repeated header block. Rows 14, 30, 33, 36, 41 and 42 are redacted: the activity label is covered by a black bar carrying the red label 'CCI'. They are transcribed as printed ('CCI') and still carry their marks; no attempt was made to recover the hidden names. Rows 41 and 42 sit under one black bar with the 'CCI' label printed once across the boundary between them; the Comment-column rule lines (y=486.4 / 500.2 / 514.1 pt on document page 45) confirm they are two separate rows, each with its own X at ETV. Row 42's label cell carries no text layer at all, so its cell_text is empty and the name was read visually from the shared bar. Rows 6-9 (Concomitant medications, Adverse events, Review modified Mayo score (MMS), Tobacco use) precede the first shaded section header and therefore have no parent; they are given indentation_level 1 like every other mark-carrying row, because level 0 is reserved here for the shaded/bold organizational rows that carry no marks. Indentation is signalled by grey shading and bold rather than by leading whitespace, hence indentation_method=font_signal throughout. No merged marks, spanning arrows or vertically merged marks occur in this table; every mark is a single 'X' in a single column. The abbreviations block on document page 46 yields no annotations: none of its terms is printed as a marker on a grid cell, a header cell or an activity label (section 6)."
 },
